#. Tag: title
#: sync.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Syncing your &handheld; with a PC"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This chapter describes the synchronization process that &kpilot; uses, "
"focusing on the &kpilot; daemon functionality. You may sync your &handheld; "
"using the <link linkend=\"builtin\">internal viewers</link> and / or <link "
"linkend=\"conduits\">conduits</link>, depending on your personal "
"preferences. Conduits allow external applications to interface with the data "
"on your &handheld;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is a good idea to make a <link linkend=\"backup\">backup</link> of your "
"&handheld; regularly. Other than making backups, it should rarely be "
"necessary to do anything other than drop your &handheld; on the cradle and "
"press the &HotSync; button. The &kpilot; daemon icon in the system tray will "
"flash indicating that a sync is under way."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: sync.docbook:23 sync.docbook:237 sync.docbook:274
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpilot; Daemon Pop-Up Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: sync.docbook:26 sync.docbook:240 sync.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&kpilot; daemon popup menu</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:27 sync.docbook:241 sync.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>&kpilot; daemon popup menu</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To which type of sync &kpilot; will perform next, you can use the main "
"application <link linkend=\"menu-file\"> <menuchoice> <guimenu>File</"
"guimenu> </menuchoice> menu</link>, or right click the &kpilot; daemon icon "
"located in the system tray, and select one of the menu items under the "
"<menuchoice> <guisubmenu>Next Sync</guisubmenu> </menuchoice> sub menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you hover over the &kpilot; daemon icon, a tooltip will appear showing "
"you what the type of sync &kpilot; will perform next."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid "In short, the sync types are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>HotSync (once)</guilabel>: this option offers a nice balance "
"between speed and data safety."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>FastSync (once)</guilabel>: only sync those databases that have "
"conduits."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>FullSync (once)</guilabel>: the safest option, but takes the "
"longest time to complete."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Backup (once)</guilabel>: copy all the data from the &handheld; to "
"the <acronym>PC</acronym>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Restore from Backup (once)</guilabel>: copy the data from a "
"previous backup from the PC to the &handheld;, erasing the data previously "
"held there."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:85 sync.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the restore functionality with care, as you can lose all the new data "
"entered on the &handheld; since the last backup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Copy Handheld to PC (once)</guilabel>: run all conduits and sync "
"all databases, but instead of merging the information from both sources, "
"just copy the handheld data to the PC."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use with care, as this option erases the changes you made in your PC since "
"the last sync."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Copy PC to Handheld (once)</guilabel>: run all conduits and sync "
"all databases, but instead of merging the information from both sources, "
"just copy the PC data to the handheld."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use with care, as this option erases the changes you made in your handheld "
"since the last sync."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can change the default syncing behavior of &kpilot; by "
"choosing the most suitable option in the <link linkend=\"page-hotsync"
"\">&HotSync; configure dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To configure the conduits or the sync process, you do not need to open the "
"main &kpilot; application, as the <menuchoice> <guimenuitem>Configure "
"KPilot...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> menu item is available on the &kpilot; "
"daemon popup menu as well."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: sync.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "Backing up your &handheld; data"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On every backup, &kpilot; stores a copy of all your &handheld; data under "
"the <filename class=\"directory\">$KDEHOME/share/apps/kpilot/DBBackup/User "
"Name/</filename> folder, allowing you to restore that copy later, if needed. "
"The <filename class=\"directory\">$KDEHOME</filename> environment variable "
"(typically <filename class=\"directory\">/home/Login Name/.kde/</filename>) "
"points to the folder that contains your configuration and data for the &kde; "
"applications."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is a good idea to backup your data often. To perform a backup, you can "
"click the <menuchoice> <guisubmenu>Next Sync</guisubmenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Backup</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> on the &kpilot; daemon icon "
"popup menu or the <menuchoice> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Backup</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice> menu item on the main &kpilot; application menu "
"in order to make the next sync a backup. Then, just press the &HotSync; "
"button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: sync.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restoring Your &handheld; Data"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The restore operation consist of transferring all the data previously saved "
"on the <acronym>PC</acronym> to the &handheld;, effectively erasing all the "
"new data held by the device by returning it to a previous state."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The data saved on the last backup is located on the <filename class="
"\"directory\">$KDEHOME/share/apps/kpilot/DBBackup/User Name/</filename> "
"folder. The <filename class=\"directory\">$KDEHOME</filename> environment "
"variable (typically <filename class=\"directory\">/home/Login Name/.kde/</"
"filename>) points to the folder that contains your configuration and data "
"for the &kde; applications."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The most common use for the restore functionality is to recover from a "
"hardware or software failure on the device. The restore function can be "
"accessed from the main &kpilot; application, and from the &kpilot; daemon. "
"be careful, as restoring the data is not a common operation. In order to "
"restore the data at the next sync, click the <menuchoice> <guimenu>File</"
"guimenu> <guimenuitem>Restore</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> menu item, then "
"press the &HotSync; button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: sync.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selecting the Synchronization Type"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are three ways to sync your &handheld;, <guilabel>HotSync</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>FastSync</guilabel> or <guilabel>FullSync</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you press the &HotSync; button on your &handheld;, &kpilot;'s will run "
"the default sync operation (usually a <guilabel>HotSync</guilabel>). You can "
"select the default sync operation in the <link linkend=\"page-hotsync"
"\">&HotSync; configure dialog</link>. Alternatively, you can click one of "
"the sync options on the main &kpilot; application <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> </menuchoice> menu or on the &kpilot; daemon popup "
"<menuchoice> <guisubmenu>Next Sync</guisubmenu> </menuchoice> submenu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the <link linkend=\"page-hotsync\">&HotSync; configure dialog</link> "
"is the only way to change the default sync operation. The main &kpilot; "
"application <menuchoice> <guimenu>File</guimenu> </menuchoice> menu items or "
"the &kpilot; daemon popup <menuchoice> <guisubmenu>Next Sync</guisubmenu> </"
"menuchoice> submenu items change only the type of sync that will be "
"performed <emphasis>next</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information on the sync types, please refer to the descriptions "
"available in <xref linkend=\"page-hotsync\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: sync.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid "Syncing your &handheld; Data Using Conduits"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Conduits are programs that interface your &handheld; data with <acronym>PC</"
"acronym> applications or sync your &handheld; data with files that can be "
"used by <acronym>PC</acronym> applications."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Conduits can be set up by selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Configure KPilot...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>, or using the "
"daemon pop up menu and clicking the <guimenuitem>Configure KPilot...</"
"guimenuitem> menu item."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Conduits</guilabel> tree in the configuration dialog collects "
"all the installed conduits available. The conduits can be enabled and "
"disabled by clicking on the check box to the left of the conduit's name. "
"Conduits can have an extensive configuration of their own, and may be "
"supplied by third parties. Most of the conduits require some initial "
"configuration, so it is strongly recommended to check the <link linkend="
"\"config-conduits\">section detailing the default conduits configuration</"
"link> before using them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid "The default conduits are the following:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: sync.docbook:304
#, no-c-format
msgid "KNotes / Memos"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid "Synchronizes the Memo Pad application with &knotes;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:308
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The conduit only synchronizes the Memo Pad data if &knotes; is running. If "
"you want to enable this functionality, please remember to start &knotes; "
"first, or check if it is already running (tip: look for the &knotes; icon in "
"the system tray)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: sync.docbook:319
#, no-c-format
msgid "Notepad"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:321
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Exports the free hand notes of the &handheld;'s Notepad application as "
"pictures to the PC."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: sync.docbook:330
#, no-c-format
msgid "Time Synchronization"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets the &handheld;'s time to that of the desktop machine. Useful for "
"keeping the clock of the &handheld; accurate."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: sync.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid "Calendar (KOrganizer)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Synchronizes the Datebook application with &korganizer; or with a iCalendar "
"file of your choice."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: sync.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid "Palm DOC"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:347
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Automatically converts, installs and sync text files in the &PalmPilot; DOC "
"format, so you can read the text files with most DOC-capable applications on "
"the &handheld;. There are many free or open source Palm DOC readers, and "
"some Palm DOC editors for your handheld."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Any plain text file can be easily converted. For instance, you can download "
"and convert the public domain books provided by the <ulink url=\"http://www."
"gutenberg.net\"> Gutenberg Project</ulink> and read them in your &handheld;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: sync.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid "Addressbook"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Synchronizes the Address application with &kaddressbook; or with a vCard "
"file of your choice."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: sync.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid "System Information"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Writes information about your &handheld;, (such as OS version, RAM "
"available, and the list of databases) to a file. Useful mostly for debugging "
"purposes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: sync.docbook:377
#, no-c-format
msgid "ToDo's (KOrganizer)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:378
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Synchronizes the Todo list application with &korganizer; or with a iCalendar "
"file of your choice."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: sync.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid "MAL (AvantGo) Conduit"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Synchronizes your &handheld; with the &AvantGo; server. The &AvantGo; server "
"offers general content (news, guides, stock quotes, &etc;) in a format that "
"is suitable for reading in a &handheld;. To use this conduit, you need to "
"register, subscribe the channels you select and install the &AvantGo; "
"software on your &handheld;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: sync.docbook:396
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mail"
msgstr "Corrièl"

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:397
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sends mail written on the &handheld; through &kmail;. There is no provision "
"for receiving mail, however."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: sync.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid "Perl"
msgstr "Perl"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: sync.docbook:405
#, no-c-format
msgid "Python"
msgstr "Python"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: sync.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid "NULL"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:407
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These conduits are intended as a programming demonstration, and serve no "
"practical purpose during a &HotSync;. They are not normally listed, but you "
"may see them on some systems."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: sync.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The Conduit Setup Dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: sync.docbook:420
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The Conduit Setup Dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:421
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>The Conduit Setup Dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: sync.docbook:429
#, no-c-format
msgid "Resolving Conflicts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Data records can be changed both on the &handheld; and on the <acronym>PC</"
"acronym>. If one record has incompatible changes in both the &handheld; and "
"the <acronym>PC</acronym>, (such as changing a phone number in different "
"ways on both sides), the conflicting change needs to be resolved so that "
"both the &handheld; and the <acronym>PC</acronym> are in sync again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: sync.docbook:440
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A popup dialog may appear, asking you how to resolve the conflict, or you "
"may have a general rule to automatically handle these conflicts (depending "
"on your <link linkend=\"page-hotsync\">conflict resolution choice</link>). "
"Note that you can define different resolution choices for different conduits "
"in the <link linkend=\"config-conduits\">conduits configuration dialog</"
"link>."
msgstr ""
